  {
   "class": "VERIFIED",
   "text": "Software-GL runs (no DRM device in the WebProcess) show rafA->rafB p50 34-37 ms; the GPU-enabled run (WebProcess opened /dev/dri/renderD128 xe and its render-engine cycle counter increased) shows 6-11 ms, with diagnostic group-start medians of 40-41 ms for the basic documents."
  },
  {
   "class": "VERIFIED",
   "text": "In software-GL runs the task posted in rafA often ran only after rafB (see taskARanAfterRafB), so rafA->taskA is not a rendering-update duration."
  },
  {
   "class": "INFERRED",
   "text": "The graphics path materially affects post-revision frame latency."
  },
  {
   "class": "UNVERIFIED",
   "text": "Whether the software-GL cost is main-thread painting, compositor/display pacing or another browser-internal step; exact GPU execution time; equivalence of the Xvfb-presented GPU configuration to a physical display."
  },
  {
   "class": "WITHDRAWN",
   "text": "Earlier statement \"frame wait p50 0 ms, so the delay is main-thread drawing, not compositor waiting\" (t010-native-completeness REPORT section 7) is not supported by the observer design."
  }
 ]
